tmux reduced to browser-style tabs.
run many coding agents at once and keep them alive across ssh disconnects.

┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 1 shell   2 codex   3 pi  [4 claude]     ^B a agents  ^B t shell │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ╭─ Claude Code ────────────────────────────────────────────────╮ │
│ │                                                              │ │
│ │                     Welcome back Yahya!                      │ │
│ │                                                              │ │
│ │                           ▐▛███▜▌                            │ │
│ │                          ▝▜█████▛▘                           │ │
│ │                            ▘▘ ▝▝                             │ │
│ │                                                              │ │
│ │               Opus 5 (1M context) with xhig…                 │ │
│ │                         Claude Max                           │ │
│ │                            ~/dev                             │ │
│ │                                                              │ │
│ ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯ │
│                                                                  │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ ❯ Try "how does tmux work?"                                      │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│   ⏵⏵ bypass permissions on (shift+tab to cycle) · ← for agents   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

works on mac and linux with bash, curl and tmux 3.0 or newer.

install to `~/.local/bin/tabs`:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/install.sh | bash

make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your path, then run `tabs`. update with:

    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/update.sh | bash

from a clone, use `./install.sh` or `./update.sh`.

a failed download leaves the installed copy intact.

keys (press `ctrl+b`, then the letter or arrow):

    t          new shell in the current tab's directory
    a          choose claude, codex, pi or opencode
    g          show the full current directory
    w          close tab
    ← / →      previous / next tab

new tabs use the current directory. claude and codex create worktrees in git repos.
claude bypasses permissions; codex uses yolo mode. tab names show the agent and directory.
`ctrl+t` and `ctrl+n` also open the agent menu when the terminal passes them to tmux.
run `tabs --reload` after updating to apply keys to an active session.

to use `tabs` when you type `tmux`, add `alias tmux=tabs` to your shell config.
`command tmux` still runs the real tmux.
